-- title:
--   Order of p-torsion in Pic⁰ over ℂ
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, and assume: (i) there is an $x \in F$ transcendental over $\mathbb{C}$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}(x)$ generated by $x$; (ii) `IsCurveOver ℂ F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ (a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the places of $F/\mathbb{C}$, a place being a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$ and being a principal ideal ring) with $D(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for all $v$ and $\deg D = 0$, the residue field of each place is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$; (iii) `HasCanonicalDivisor`, i.e. every nonzero $\omega \in \Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}}$ admits a divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}$ of the differential coefficient of $\omega$ at $v$. Let $p$ be a natural number assumed prime. Then the $p$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/\mathbb{C})$, defined as the $\mathbb{Z}$-torsion by $p$ of the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors by the subgroup of principal divisors, has cardinality $p^{2g}$, where $g =$ `genus ℂ F` is $\lfloor (\deg K + 2)/2 \rfloor$ computed from a canonical divisor $K$ attached to some nonzero differential (and $0$ if $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}} = 0$). In particular the statement asserts finiteness of this torsion subgroup, since `Nat.card` returns $p^{2g} \neq 0$.
--
--   This is the transcendental count of $p$-torsion on the Jacobian of a compact Riemann surface: for the function field of a complex curve of genus $g$ one has $J[p] \cong (\mathbb{Z}/p)^{2g}$, classically obtained from Abel's theorem and Jacobi inversion. It serves as the constant-field $\mathbb{C}$ case from which the corresponding statement over an arbitrary algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, and the finiteness of torsion in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, are deduced.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_natCard_torsion_prime_eq_pow_genus_complex.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_CanonicalDivisor

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.natCard_torsion_prime_eq_pow_genus_complex (F : Type*) [Field F]
    [Algebra ℂ F]
    (hfg : ∃ x : F, Transcendental ℂ x ∧ FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin ℂ ({x} : Set F)) F)
    [IsCurveOver ℂ F] [HasCanonicalDivisor (K := ℂ) (F := F)]
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] :
    Nat.card (Pic0.torsion ℂ F p) = p ^ (2 * genus ℂ F) := by sorry
